    {
      "id": "7460974265266064686",
      "kind": "organic",
      "url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@nicksaquariums/video/7460974265266064686",
      "caption": "“How I Cleaned My Calcium-Deposited Fish Tank! 🐟✨” Is your old fish tank covered in stubborn calcium deposits and looking foggy? Don’t worry—here’s my tried-and-true method to make it sparkle again! 💦 1️⃣ Empty the Tank: First, I removed everything—fish, substrate, decor—and rinsed the tank thoroughly. Never clean the tank with fish inside! 2️⃣ Vinegar Solution: I mixed equal parts warm water and white vinegar. Vinegar is natural, non-toxic, and super effective at breaking down calcium buildup. (Avoid using harsh chemicals—they can harm your fish!) 3️⃣ Scrape Gently: Using an edge razor, I carefully scraped the calcium deposits off the glass. Be patient and work gently to avoid scratching. Pro tip: Hold the razor at a 45-degree angle for better control. 4️⃣ Scrub Away: For the stubborn spots, I used a scrubber dipped in the vinegar solution. Circular motions worked best for me. 5️⃣ Rinse Thoroughly: Once the glass was spotless, I rinsed the tank multiple times with warm water to ensure no vinegar residue was left behind. 6️⃣ Final Touch: After drying, I added fresh substrate, decor, and conditioned water—and it was good as new! This simple method brought my old tank back to life without breaking the bank or compromising my fish’s safety. 🌿✨ Got any stubborn tank-cleaning tips of your own? Let me know in the comments!👇 #FishTankCleaning #AquariumCare #Fishkeeping #AquariumTips #CrystalClearAquarium #FishkeeperLife#CapCut ",
